even if  it's as as little as one hour day just  to start building up some momentum with  your company and that fuels you to want  to keep going so you don't have to start  full time start part-time talk to your  customers get close to them make sure  you're building a product or service  that really help solve their problems  and continue to building around that the  last part again to also make sure you're  reducing your risk is don't spend money  in till you're making money whatever  business you're in usually don't have to  spend a lot of mine  to get it started and you can start  especially if you're doing a service  type of based business the only amount  that you have to invest is your time and  I encourage entrepreneurs not to focus  on how much resources you have but how  resourceful you can be and that's going  to be what determines your success so  don't start spend a lot of money that's  what's scary right you're going to lose  whatever nest egg you built up for  yourself spend a lot of time building it  up talking to customers getting close to  them understanding their pain point  seeing where you might be able to help  and then as money starts coming in from  small sales that you're able to make  then you can invest that back into your  business and you have cash flow to start  supporting your company and eventually  you can get to the point where you can  quit whatever job you have whatever  other income sources you have to take up  your time to focus on your own company  so get excited about what you're doing  let that fuel you let that kind of get  you going get your juices pumped up to  want to get that business launched  remember you don't have to start full  time you can start on a part-time basis  and don't spend a lot of money don't  spend until you're making money try to  focus on making that money first before  you start letting the flow out of your  wall because anybody can spend but not  everybody can earn so that should be  your focus hopefully you guys like the  video if you did please give it a thumbs  up if you have other questions or other  comments for Liz it'd be great to see it  in the comments below and again if  you're Canadian entrepreneur who wants  to enter the contest to win a hundred  thousand dollars go to the bill mail com  / the challenge I'm one of the judges so  hopefully we'll see you there thank you  and stay tuned for next episode  you
 

